manual.name.3025a3fcc4bac634afbd=Mechanical shaft
manual.item.3025a3fcc4bac634afbd.description=Transmits rotation through aligned ends.
manual.item.3025a3fcc4bac634afbd.operation=Placement follows the clicked face. Sneak-interact to cycle X/Y/Z.
manual.item.3025a3fcc4bac634afbd.energy=Generates no power and adds no stress. Needs a connected source.
manual.item.3025a3fcc4bac634afbd.example=Connect the water wheel to the large gear in the tutorial.
manual.item.3025a3fcc4bac634afbd.errors=A perpendicular axle or a gap disconnects the network.
manual.name.6f3cec468dc5784e7454=Small gear
manual.item.6f3cec468dc5784e7454.description=Small gear for transmission and speed changes.
manual.item.6f3cec468dc5784e7454.operation=Adjacent coplanar small gears reverse rotation. Large/small gears mesh diagonally in their shared plane.
manual.item.6f3cec468dc5784e7454.energy=No own stress; ratios change RPM and downstream demand.
manual.item.6f3cec468dc5784e7454.example=After a large gear it turns twice as fast in reverse.
manual.item.6f3cec468dc5784e7454.errors=A large/small pair sharing only a lateral face does not mesh.
manual.name.5f8c1c92541588133fed=Large gear
manual.item.5f8c1c92541588133fed.description=Large gear with diagonal transmission.
manual.item.5f8c1c92541588133fed.operation=Large→small: -2. Small→large: -0.5. Perpendicular large gears use an axis diagonal.
manual.item.5f8c1c92541588133fed.energy=No own stress. Networks stop above 256 RPM.
manual.item.5f8c1c92541588133fed.example=An 8 RPM wheel can produce -16 RPM through a large→small pair.
manual.item.5f8c1c92541588133fed.errors=Contradictory ratio cycles stop the entire network.
manual.name.dd36d13261a5b60e7de4=Gearbox
manual.item.dd36d13261a5b60e7de4.description=Gearbox for changing the transmission axis.
manual.item.dd36d13261a5b60e7de4.operation=The selected axis blocks two faces; the other four are ports. Direction depends on the port pair.
manual.item.dd36d13261a5b60e7de4.energy=Generates no capacity and consumes no stress.
manual.item.dd36d13261a5b60e7de4.example=Select Y to connect X and Z branches.
manual.item.dd36d13261a5b60e7de4.errors=Trying to connect through a blocked-axis face does not work.
manual.name.2e382f879c5a4db31ca1=Water wheel
manual.item.2e382f879c5a4db31ca1.description=Source driven by a verifiable falling-water condition.
manual.item.2e382f879c5a4db31ca1.operation=X axle: falling water at Z±; Z axle: at X±. Side water needs liquid_depth ≥ 8 and water above.
manual.item.2e382f879c5a4db31ca1.energy=Generates ±8 RPM and 256 SU. Y axle is disabled.
manual.item.2e382f879c5a4db31ca1.example=Use the tutorial glass channel; Z+ falling water with an X axle gives +8 RPM.
manual.item.2e382f879c5a4db31ca1.errors=Still water, no water above, lava or balanced opposing sides do not generate rotation. This does not reproduce all Java flow rules.
manual.name.a91ec770560f956024cd=Test source (development)
manual.item.a91ec770560f956024cd.description=Configurable development source.
manual.item.a91ec770560f956024cd.operation=Interact to cycle off, positive RPM and negative RPM. Sneaking changes the axis.
manual.item.a91ec770560f956024cd.energy=Signed 8/16/32/64 RPM; capacity is 32 SU per RPM.
manual.item.a91ec770560f956024cd.example=Test a dry network, then switch it off to return to water power.
manual.item.a91ec770560f956024cd.errors=Incompatible sources stop the network. Its recipe is not final survival balance.
manual.name.7b618b56d3e66d7ef56f=Speed gauge
manual.item.7b618b56d3e66d7ef56f.description=Measures effective server-graph RPM.
manual.item.7b618b56d3e66d7ef56f.operation=Connect through its axle. Look at it nearby to read the action bar and needle.
manual.item.7b618b56d3e66d7ef56f.energy=Passive: adds no stress.
manual.item.7b618b56d3e66d7ef56f.example=Verify -16 RPM after the tutorial large→small pair.
manual.item.7b618b56d3e66d7ef56f.errors=0 RPM can mean no source, recalculation, overload, conflict or an unavailable chunk; read the state.
manual.name.bfaba9f4bcbed939bc35=Stress gauge / brake
manual.item.bfaba9f4bcbed939bc35.description=Measures demand and capacity; includes a test brake.
manual.item.bfaba9f4bcbed939bc35.operation=Interact to cycle a 0/8/64 SU per RPM brake; sneaking changes the axis.
manual.item.bfaba9f4bcbed939bc35.energy=Passive at 0. The brake consumes its coefficient × absolute theoretical RPM.
manual.item.bfaba9f4bcbed939bc35.example=At -16 RPM, brake 8 demands 128 SU; brake 64 demands 1024 SU and overloads one wheel.
manual.item.bfaba9f4bcbed939bc35.errors=The brake is a Bedrock test extension, not a production machine or the full passive Java behavior.
manual.name.5a5820af58585ae582b3=Gear component
manual.item.5a5820af58585ae582b3.description=Intermediate small-gear component.
manual.item.5a5820af58585ae582b3.operation=Craft and assemble at a crafting table; see recipes and uses.
manual.item.5a5820af58585ae582b3.energy=No kinetic power required.
manual.item.5a5820af58585ae582b3.example=Craft a gear from this component.
manual.item.5a5820af58585ae582b3.errors=Do not confuse an inventory component with a rotating block.
manual.name.f3cc680879e47ac04470=Shaft component
manual.item.f3cc680879e47ac04470.description=Intermediate shaft component.
manual.item.f3cc680879e47ac04470.operation=Craft and assemble at a crafting table; see recipes and uses.
manual.item.f3cc680879e47ac04470.energy=No kinetic power required.
manual.item.f3cc680879e47ac04470.example=Assemble it into a shaft for the first circuit.
manual.item.f3cc680879e47ac04470.errors=The component cannot be placed as a shaft until assembled.
manual.name.b16367058b1f2ed1bb6c=Mechanical Engineering Manual
manual.item.b16367058b1f2ed1bb6c.description=Mechanical Engineering Manual: add-on recipes, uses, references and tutorials.
manual.item.b16367058b1f2ed1bb6c.operation=Use the book to open it. Search in Spanish/English or filter categories. Back preserves the navigation path.
manual.item.b16367058b1f2ed1bb6c.energy=Browsing consumes no power or ingredients.
manual.item.b16367058b1f2ed1bb6c.example=Start with the wheel, shafts and gears tutorial.
manual.item.b16367058b1f2ed1bb6c.errors=Java references are not Bedrock recipes. Partially available means code/JSON exists with in-game verification pending.
manual.name.4a52cee0cf8003d3a5e7=Mechanical press
manual.item.4a52cee0cf8003d3a5e7.description=Kinetically powered press using a vanilla barrel underneath as input and output.
manual.item.4a52cee0cf8003d3a5e7.operation=Place a barrel directly underneath, connect a horizontal X/Z shaft and insert plain ingots. The batch transforms in the same slot after completion. Forms never insert or remove items.
manual.item.4a52cee0cf8003d3a5e7.energy=Impact of 8 SU per RPM. Cycle of 240 work units per ingot; speed accelerates work following Java PressingBehaviour.
manual.item.4a52cee0cf8003d3a5e7.example=An 8 RPM wheel supplies 256 SU; the press demands 64 SU. One ingot needs 240 active ticks; batches take proportionally longer.
manual.item.4a52cee0cf8003d3a5e7.errors=No power, barrel or valid input means no output. Moving or changing a batch can reset progress. Named or custom-data items are not processed. In-engine crafting remains untested.
manual.name.f484d6e683f21877d382=Iron sheet
manual.item.f484d6e683f21877d382.description=Sheet obtained by pressing iron.
manual.item.f484d6e683f21877d382.operation=See the pressing recipe and place its ingot in the barrel underneath a powered press.
manual.item.f484d6e683f21877d382.energy=Requires a powered press, not a crafting table.
manual.item.f484d6e683f21877d382.example=One plain ingot is replaced by one sheet in the same slot.
manual.item.f484d6e683f21877d382.errors=A same-named Java reference does not add another recipe. Named, lore-bearing or custom-property iron is not converted.
