manual.tutorial.first_network=First network: wheel, shafts and gears
manual.tutorial.first_network.0.title=Prepare materials
manual.tutorial.first_network.0.body=Read the linked recipes and craft the wheel, shafts, gears and gauges. These are original add-on recipes.
manual.tutorial.first_network.1.title=Orient the wheel
manual.tutorial.first_network.1.body=Place an X-axis wheel. East/west faces select X; sneak-interact cycles X/Y/Z.
manual.tutorial.first_network.2.title=Make water fall
manual.tutorial.first_network.2.body=Build a channel that drops water on the wheel’s Z+ side and keeps water directly above. Still water does not work. Look at the wheel when checking: it must have effective rotation.
manual.tutorial.first_network.3.title=Connect shafts
manual.tutorial.first_network.3.body=Place two shafts toward X+ from the wheel, aligned end to end. Look at a connected shaft when checking.
manual.tutorial.first_network.4.title=Change speed
manual.tutorial.first_network.4.body=Place a large gear at the end and a small gear one block up and one toward Z+; both X-axis. Large→small should give -16 RPM from the +8 wheel.
manual.tutorial.first_network.5.title=Measure and reproduce the scene
manual.tutorial.first_network.5.body=Connect a speed gauge through a shaft and inspect its reading. The documented scene can be placed with /function bedrockworks/kinetic_demo ONLY in a backed-up test world with an empty X[-1,8],Y[0,4],Z[-1,4] volume relative to the executor. The guide does not execute that command.
manual.tutorial.overload=Detect and recover from overload
manual.tutorial.overload.0.title=Read stress
manual.tutorial.overload.0.body=Connect a stress gauge after a large→small conversion. Each normal interaction cycles a 0/8/64 SU per RPM brake.
manual.tutorial.overload.1.title=Apply the brake
manual.tutorial.overload.1.body=With one wheel and a -16 RPM output, select brake 64. Its 1024 SU demand exceeds 256 SU and should stop the network.
manual.tutorial.overload.2.title=Recover the network
manual.tutorial.overload.2.body=Set the brake to 0 or reduce demand. Check rotation again. The brake is a Bedrock test extension, not a Java industrial machine.
manual.tutorial.disconnect=Safely split a network
manual.tutorial.disconnect.0.title=Running network
manual.tutorial.disconnect.0.body=Start with a wheel connected through several shafts to a gauge. The check requires looking at a running gauge.
manual.tutorial.disconnect.1.title=Break the bridge
manual.tutorial.disconnect.1.body=Break an intermediate shaft between source and gauge. Wait for recalculation and look at the gauge in the sourceless half; it should be idle.
manual.tutorial.disconnect.2.title=Reconnect
manual.tutorial.disconnect.2.body=Replace the shaft with the correct axis. The check requires the gauge to recover actual rotation.
manual.tutorial.first_factory=First sheet factory without commands
manual.tutorial.first_factory.0.title=Materials and recipes
manual.tutorial.first_factory.0.body=Craft a press, wheel, two shafts, two funnels and three barrels using the linked recipes. No commands or development source are needed. Prepare one unmodified iron ingot.
manual.tutorial.first_factory.1.title=Place the press
manual.tutorial.first_factory.1.body=Use the press at (0,2,0) as origin. Put a barrel directly below at (0,1,0), shafts at (1,2,0) and (2,2,0), and a wheel at (3,2,0). Align all axles to X. Look at the press to check placement.
manual.tutorial.first_factory.2.title=Water power
manual.tutorial.first_factory.2.body=Make water fall on the Z+ side of the wheel, with water above the falling cell. Contain the channel. The press should receive 8 RPM and draw 64 SU from the wheel’s 256 SU; look at the press when checking.
manual.tutorial.first_factory.3.title=Input and output
manual.tutorial.first_factory.3.body=At Y=1 place barrels at X=2 and X=-2, and west-facing funnels at X=1 and X=-1. With an empty hand, sneak-interact to rotate; normal interaction switches mode. Set X=1 to input and X=-1 to output.
manual.tutorial.first_factory.4.title=Produce and collect
manual.tutorial.first_factory.4.body=Put one iron ingot in the X=2 barrel. The funnel moves it below the press. In a small factory at 8 RPM, one ingot needs 240 processing visits (~12 seconds at 20 TPS), plus transport waits. Collect an iron sheet from X=-2. Delivery must be checked manually; the guide does not verify inventories.
manual.tutorial.first_factory.5.title=Safe stops
manual.tutorial.first_factory.5.body=Repeat with copper and gold. Break a shaft during processing: input should remain and progress should pause. Reconnect. Fill the output barrel: products should remain below the press. Do not add ingots to the active slot: changing the stack resets its work.
